##

00:00:00.226 --> 00:00:02.498 line:91%
We've just shot
my first parkour video.

00:00:02.498 --> 00:00:04.021 line:85%
Lower your expectations.

00:00:04.021 --> 00:00:05.876 line:91%
But that means
I need to give you the disclaimer.

00:00:05.876 --> 00:00:08.539
This is Hedge,
a qualified parkour instructor,

00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:12.853 position:67%
and also one of the people who writes
the qualifications for parkour instructors.

00:00:13.353 --> 00:00:16.647 position:67%
<c.yellow>We've made a lot of choices, both on-camera
and off-camera, to keep Tom safe.</c>

00:00:16.647 --> 00:00:20.410 position:72% line:91%
<c.yellow>We've taught him the basics
in a safe environment, and built it up slowly.</c>

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.755 line:91%
<c.yellow>Don't try what you see at home.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>But if you do want to try it...</c>

00:00:23.755 --> 00:00:27.546 position:73% line:91%
go off somewhere with a
qualified parkour instructor, and try it there.

00:00:28.046 --> 00:00:31.188 line:91%
<i>I got an email from
Access Parkour in Edinburgh,</i>

00:00:31.188 --> 00:00:34.105 position:56% line:85%
inviting me to learn something cool.

00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:37.127 line:91%
<i>(chuckles)</i>
<c.colorEEEEEE>And now I'm here, at this—</c>

00:00:37.127 --> 00:00:39.756 line:91%
I was expecting sort of
foam pits and things.

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:42.187 line:91%
This is very solid.
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:45.887 line:91%
<c.yellow>So parkour developed outdoors.
It's an outdoor discipline.</c>

00:00:45.887 --> 00:00:48.502 line:91%
<c.yellow>And the idea is that
you challenge yourself to...</c>

00:00:48.502 --> 00:00:51.479 line:91%
<c.yellow>move through the environment
and complete challenges.</c>

00:00:51.479 --> 00:00:55.191 line:91%
<c.yellow>And so what we do here is,
when we brought it indoors,</c>

00:00:55.191 --> 00:00:58.351 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>we're replicating outdoor environments,
where everything is solid.</c>

00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:00.179 line:91%
<c.yellow>It's made of
metal, concrete, wood.</c>

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:02.556 line:91%
<c.yellow>We do have a rubber floor down,
which is there to...</c>

00:01:02.556 --> 00:01:05.680 line:91%
<c.yellow>just prevent any major spills
from causing any injury.</c>

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.694 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>But generally, the way we
try and teach you is we're gonna learn</c>

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:12.008 line:91%
<c.yellow>how to move safely
in concrete environments.</c>

00:01:12.008 --> 00:01:14.559 line:91%
<c.yellow>And everything that we do today is
going to build up on that idea.</c>

00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:16.786 line:91%
<c.yellow>So we're going to learn
how to keep ourselves safe.</c>

00:01:16.786 --> 00:01:18.452 line:91%
<c.yellow>Learn how to drop down
when there's a problem,</c>

00:01:18.452 --> 00:01:20.529 line:91%
<c.yellow>learn how to get off
from balancing,</c>

00:01:20.529 --> 00:01:24.121 line:91%
<c.yellow>and just generally
keep you, um, safe,</c>

00:01:24.121 --> 00:01:27.472 line:91%
<c.yellow>by teaching you how to fall
and how to drop down.</c>

00:01:27.472 --> 00:01:31.917 position:77% line:91%
<c.yellow>But for a beginner, we're much more interested in
challenging you at your own level.</c>

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.563 line:91%
So my level is not great.
Like I was—

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:36.803 line:85%
I— I don't really have—

00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:40.719 position:72% line:91%
I can sorta do that, and that's about the most
I can get out of upper body strength.

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:44.199 position:58% line:91%
I was kinda assuming I was gonna need
a lot more than that to do anything.

00:01:44.199 --> 00:01:48.734 line:91%
<c.yellow>Parkour is something where...
you get fit by doing it.</c>

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:52.198 line:91%
<c.yellow>Rather than— It's really common.
People say to me,</c>

00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:54.677 position:61% line:85%
<c.yellow>"Oh, I'm not fit enough to do parkour."</c>

00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:57.881 line:91%
<c.yellow>But actually, by doing parkour,
we challenge you at your level,</c>

00:01:57.881 --> 00:02:00.195 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>and you'll get stronger,
you'll learn more, you'll develop more.</c>

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:03.028 position:61% line:91%
So I'm not going to be doing big flips
through the air, or anything like that?

00:02:03.028 --> 00:02:06.246 line:85%
My goal here is that after...

00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:08.335 position:59% line:91%
What, we've got about six hours today?
<c.yellow>Yep.</c>

00:02:08.335 --> 00:02:11.920 line:91%
And then tomorrow, we go out
and we try and film something

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.835 position:56% line:91%
with the help of slow-motion cameras
and a production team...

00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:17.369 line:85%
that does not look terrible.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:20.872 line:91%
Like, if I get one shot
where I look vaguely cool...

00:02:20.872 --> 00:02:22.576 line:85%
I'm gonna be happy with that.

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:24.823 line:91%
'Cause I don't think I've ever
looked cool in my life.

00:02:24.823 --> 00:02:26.012 line:85%
<c.yellow>That seems possible.</c>

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:33.256 line:91%
<c.yellow>So, when I'm balancing...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yep.</c>

00:02:33.256 --> 00:02:35.242 line:85%
<c.yellow>I want to have my foot on,</c>

00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:39.701 position:66% line:91%
<c.yellow>but you'll see my toe is just off the bar,
and my heel is just off the bar here.</c>

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.236 line:91%
<c.yellow>and my right knee is
just on the outside.</c>

00:02:42.236 --> 00:02:45.303 position:72% line:91%
<c.yellow>So it's actually a slightly external position.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay.</c>

00:02:45.303 --> 00:02:48.158 line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, so that's the position.
If you feel strongly there,</c>

00:02:48.158 --> 00:02:51.047 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then this is nice and tight,
and this is nice and tight,</c>

00:02:51.047 --> 00:02:54.331 line:91%
<c.yellow>you come up, you balance
on a single foot, okay?</c>

00:02:54.331 --> 00:02:56.683 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>And you're gonna fall down
quite a bit right now, and that's fine.</c>

00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:00.787 line:85%
<c.yellow>Good. So, um...</c>

00:03:01.316 --> 00:03:03.446 line:91%
<c.yellow>Try and be a stick
instead of spaghetti.</c>

00:03:03.446 --> 00:03:04.854 line:91%
<c.yellow>So...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay.</c>

00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:07.455 line:91%
<c.yellow>We will stand up,
and I'm gonna try and hold tight,</c>

00:03:07.455 --> 00:03:10.097 line:68%
<c.yellow>and the work is going to be
done at the knee.</c>

00:03:10.097 --> 00:03:12.432 line:30%
<c.yellow>So everything else is tight,
and it's just the knee.</c>

00:03:12.432 --> 00:03:15.334 line:30%
<c.yellow>Everything else moving,
it's like if you imagine...</c>

00:03:16.266 --> 00:03:19.754 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>trying to coordinate
every bit of your body moving at once.</c>

00:03:19.754 --> 00:03:22.837 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>Instead, you hold your body,
and do the balance with a single joint.</c>

00:03:22.837 --> 00:03:25.896 position:86% line:68%
Okay, and that's about the right position for the foot.
<c.yellow>Stand nice and tall. Yeah.</c>

00:03:27.928 --> 00:03:29.076 line:85%
...Oh!

00:03:29.076 --> 00:03:30.867 line:91%
And there's a bit of flailing
on the arm.

00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:32.777 line:85%
<i>(laughs)</i>

00:03:34.063 --> 00:03:37.295 line:91%
As soon as— So instinctively,
I started moving my body...

00:03:37.295 --> 00:03:39.426 line:91%
and it all fell apart.
<c.yellow>Yeah?</c>

00:03:39.426 --> 00:03:42.057 line:91%
<c.yellow>Cool. Keep practicing that.
I'll be back in a second.</c>

00:03:42.057 --> 00:03:43.134 line:85%
Alright, here we go.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.750 align:start position:0% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>♪ (retro electronic dance music)</i></c>

00:03:56.107 --> 00:03:59.055 line:91%
It's the exact opposite of
